# Fraud Detection - Stratified Cross-Validation with MLflow Tracking

This repository contains an automated evaluation pipeline designed to benchmark machine learning fraud-detection candidates using **Stratified K-Fold Cross-Validation**. Every evaluation split is tracked independently in an MLflow tracking server using a **Parent-Child (Nested Run)** architecture to prevent UI dashboard clutter while maintaining deep metrics visibility.

## 📌 Project Overview
The core challenge in fraud detection modeling is handling highly imbalanced target datasets. To ensure reliable performance estimates, this script implements a 5-fold stratified splitter that preserves the balance of the target class (`roughly 70/30 split`) across all evaluation subsets. 

Instead of aggregating results into a single average score upfront, **each fold is executed inside an isolated, nested MLflow run** to capture structural drift, performance variances, and potential model instability across splits.

